00:14:30.000 --> 00:15:17.000
But today's attack, although not an isolated incident, stands out as this city's first senseless terrorist action directed at the public at large. Not yet the streets of Beirut, but a big step closer to the madness. That madness that we thought lurked only beyond our shores. The Russell Street bombing and family law court bombings were not considered linked by police. But consideration was given that the court may have been the target. The court lists were checked and recent decisions were reviewed, but nothing stood out. Others thought that maybe it was a terrorist attack, saying that Beirut had now come to Australia. A comparison made due to the Lebanese civil war that was going on at the time, where there were a lot of bombings.
但今天的袭击，虽然不是孤立事件，却因其是该市首次针对公众的毫无意义的恐怖行动而引人注目。虽然还不是贝鲁特的街道，但离那种疯狂又近了一大步。那种我们以为只潜伏在我们国界之外的疯狂。罗素街爆炸案和家庭法庭爆炸案被警方认为没有关联。但人们考虑过法院可能是目标。法院名单经过了核对，最近的判决也进行了审查，但没有发现任何异常。其他人认为这可能是一次恐怖袭击，称贝鲁特现在来到了澳大利亚。这种比较是因为当时正在进行的黎巴嫩内战，那里发生了许多爆炸事件。

26
00:15:17.000 --> 00:16:07.000
But the obvious conclusion for most was that this was an attack against the police. The bomb had been put directly outside of police headquarters, and it had been set to go off at lunchtime, ensuring that a lot of police were going to be outside the building when the bomb exploded. After all of the initial confusion had settled, a direct attack against the police was how the case was treated. Although it was on fire and damaged, the bomb car wasn't completely destroyed, and something stood out. The chassis number had been drilled out. The chassis number being the serial number of a car used to identify it. The bombers had drilled through right across the chassis number, so you could no longer see it.
但对大多数人来说，显而易见的结论是，这是一次针对警察的袭击。炸弹被直接放在警察总部外，并被设定在午餐时间引爆，以确保炸弹爆炸时会有许多警察在建筑物外。在最初的混乱平息后，此案被视为针对警察的直接袭击。虽然炸弹车着火并受损，但并没有完全摧毁，有一点很突出。底盘编号被钻掉了。底盘编号是用于识别汽车的序列号。炸弹制造者钻穿了整个底盘编号，所以你再也看不到了。

27
00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:53.000
This was very unusual, something the police hadn't seen before. The way criminals usually got rid of chassis numbers was to grind them down, or some would even try and change the numbers. Drilling through the chassis number completely was unique. Although it was completely pointless in this case, because the number plates had been left on the car. Maybe they thought the plates would be destroyed in the explosion, but they weren't, making the bomb car easily identifiable. It had been stolen two days before the bombing from the Brandon Park Shopping Centre in Mulgrave, which is about 20 kilometres or 12 miles away from Russell Street. A red and green coloured blanket was found inside the bomb car.
这非常不寻常，是警察以前从未见过的。罪犯通常销毁底盘编号的方法是将其磨掉，有些人甚至会尝试更改数字。完全钻穿底盘编号是独一无二的。尽管在这种情况下完全没有意义，因为车牌还留在车上。也许他们认为车牌会在爆炸中被摧毁，但并没有，这使得炸弹车很容易被识别。它是在爆炸发生前两天从穆尔格雷夫的布兰登公园购物中心被盗的，距离罗素街约20公里（12英里）。炸弹车内发现了一条红绿相间的毯子。

28
00:16:53.000 --> 00:17:37.000
It was burnt and damaged, but it was in okay condition considering. Good enough to be forensically tested anyway, which was important, because the blanket didn't belong to the vehicle owner. He had never seen it before. An examination revealed it contained dog hairs, belonging to a bull terrier. This could be useful to match to a suspect's dog, if a suspect was ever identified. The car was checked for fingerprints using the super glue fuming method, not the dusting method. This is where super glue is combined with water, and the vapours react with chemicals in fingerprints. But no prints were found.
它被烧毁和损坏了，但考虑到情况，状况还算可以。至少足以进行法医鉴定，这很重要，因为毯子不属于车主。他以前从未见过它。检查显示毯子上含有狗毛，属于一只斗牛梗。如果能确定嫌疑人，这对于匹配嫌疑人的狗可能很有用。警方使用强力胶熏蒸法（而不是粉末法）检查了车上的指纹。这是将强力胶与水结合，蒸汽与指纹中的化学物质发生反应的方法。但没有发现指纹。

29
00:17:37.000 --> 00:18:30.000
The search for evidence wasn't just restricted to the ground. Police from the Special Operations Group abseiled down buildings, hunting for evidence that had made its way up onto roofs and window ledges. It's on the roof of police headquarters that they found one of Constable Di Natio's boots. All of the pieces of shrapnel and all of the other evidence were bagged and taken to a large auditorium where they were catalogued. Twisted metal, bomb components, pieces of wire, the alarm clock and any other debris that was found. It was all bagged and treated with great care. The debris was basically treated like pieces of a large jigsaw puzzle that investigators would have to try and put back together. Any piece of the debris could contain valuable forensic evidence to help catch whoever was responsible.
搜寻证据不仅限于地面。特别行动小组的警察从建筑物上垂降，搜寻飞到屋顶和窗台上的证据。他们在警察总部的屋顶上发现了迪纳迪奥警员的一只靴子。所有的弹片和所有其他证据都被装袋，并带到一个大礼堂进行分类。扭曲的金属、炸弹组件、电线碎片、闹钟以及发现的任何其他碎片。一切都被装袋并小心处理。这些碎片基本上被当作大型拼图的碎片，调查人员必须设法将它们拼凑起来。任何碎片都可能包含有价值的法医证据，以帮助抓住肇事者。

30
00:18:30.000 --> 00:19:32.000
To help with the cataloging, a large grid was placed over a map of the blast zone, and every piece of evidence was marked with a letter corresponding to where it was found on that grid. Five days after the explosion, Constable Di Natio was recovering from surgery, which had been successful. He was interviewed, but he wasn't able to assist with the investigation. He didn't see anyone or anything suspicious. Constable Angela Taylor was still in a critical condition and was fighting for her life. Although there were still no suspects, the investigation was coming along. Some of the debris from the blast had now been identified as being bread crates. Investigators had worked out the main part of the bomb had been placed onto a bread crate. Then the metal tools and sockets were placed on the crate around the bomb.
为了协助分类，在爆炸区域的地图上放置了一个大网格，每一件证据都标有字母，对应于它在网格上的发现位置。爆炸发生五天后，迪纳迪奥警员手术成功，正在康复中。他接受了采访，但无法协助调查。他没有看到任何可疑的人或事。安吉拉·泰勒警员仍处于危急状态，正在为生命而战。虽然还没有嫌疑人，但调查正在取得进展。爆炸中的一些碎片现在已被确认为面包板条箱。调查人员推断炸弹的主要部分被放置在一个面包板条箱上。然后金属工具和套筒被放置在板条箱上，围绕着炸弹。

31
00:19:32.000 --> 00:20:13.000
And they knew where the bread crates came from. They were stolen during a robbery from a milk bar at Brayside, another suburb of Melbourne, about 26 kilometres or 16 miles southeast of Russell Street. The robbery occurred six weeks before the bombing. A large amount of cigarettes and confectionery were stolen along with the bread crates. There were no suspects for the robbery. A task force was established to investigate the bombing. It was made up of over 30 detectives, brought in from all different areas of Melbourne, making sure they were drawing on knowledge of possible suspects from across the entire city.
他们知道面包板条箱的来源。它们是在墨尔本另一个郊区布雷赛德的一家牛奶吧被抢劫时偷走的，距离罗素街约26公里（16英里）。抢劫发生在爆炸前六周。除了面包板条箱外，还偷走了大量的香烟和糖果。抢劫案没有嫌疑人。警方成立了一个特别工作组来调查爆炸案。它由来自墨尔本各地的30多名侦探组成，确保他们能够利用整个城市对可能嫌疑人的了解。

32
00:20:13.000 --> 00:21:05.000
As well as local detectives, members from the Arson Squad, Major Crime Squad and Homicide Squad were called in to assist. They felt there weren't a lot of people that would be capable of the attack. There was one thing to hate the police. There was another level altogether to bomb police headquarters. It didn't take long for the task force to link the bombing to a break-in that occurred six months earlier, on the 6th of October 1985. A country mine was broken into near Blackwood, about 70 kilometres or 43 miles northwest of Melbourne. A large amount of detonators and gelling night were stolen, and those detonators and gelling night were used in the Russell Street bombing. There were no leads and no suspects for the break-in.
除了当地侦探外，纵火组、重案组和凶杀组的成员也被召集来协助。他们认为没有多少人有能力进行这种袭击。憎恨警察是一回事，炸毁警察总部则是完全不同的层面。特别工作组很快将爆炸案与六个月前，即1985年10月6日发生的一起入室盗窃案联系起来。墨尔本西北约70公里（43英里）处的布莱克伍德附近的一个乡村矿场被闯入。大量雷管和胶质炸药被盗，而这些雷管和胶质炸药被用于罗素街爆炸案。那起入室盗窃案没有线索，也没有嫌疑人。

33
00:21:05.000 --> 00:22:00.000
The first lead for police happened when an unnamed male caller got in contact with the Victorian Police Commissioner. The caller said he knew who the bombers were, and he even had photos of them. He ended up calling in on five separate occasions, and he eventually said that he wanted US$500,000 in a Swiss bank account before he would tell police what he knew. The calls were traced to a number of public phone boxes in the St Kilda area, which is only a short distance away from Russell Street. Police weren't sure if the caller was genuine, or if it was just a hoax, but they couldn't ignore it. So the police commissioner was able to convince the government to offer a reward of $500,000. Not US dollars, and the money wouldn't be put in a Swiss bank account, but it was hoped it would be enough to entice the unknown caller to make contact again.
警方的第一个线索来自一名未透露姓名的男性拨打给维多利亚州警察局长的电话。打电话的人说他知道炸弹客是谁，甚至还有他们的照片。他最终打了五次电话，最后说他想要50万美元存入瑞士银行账户，才会告诉警方他所知道的情况。电话被追踪到圣基尔达地区的几个公用电话亭，距离罗素街只有很短的距离。警方不确定打电话的人是否真实，还是只是恶作剧，但他们不能忽视。因此，警察局长成功说服政府悬赏50万美元。不是美元，钱也不会存入瑞士银行账户，但希望这足以诱使那个不知名的人再次联系。

34
00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:05.000
Premier John Kane and Chief Commissioner Mick Miller jointly announced the record $500,000 reward. But in a press conference, they refused to answer any questions on developments behind their decision. The offer of an amount of this magnitude might succeed in producing vital information. And I don't propose to divulge the nature of that information in case it might jeopardise this development. Police staked out phone boxes in the St Kilda area in the hope that the caller wouldn't be able to resist the huge reward. While waiting to hear from him again, police received hundreds of other calls from members of the public. Did it work? Find out next week in Part 2 of Russell Street, here on Case 4. Thank you. There aren't comments yet for this episode. Click on any sentence in the transcript to leave a comment.
州长约翰·凯恩和警察总长米克·米勒共同宣布了50万美元的创纪录悬赏。但在新闻发布会上，他们拒绝回答有关其决定背后进展的任何问题。“提供如此巨额的赏金可能会成功获得重要信息。我不打算透露这些信息的性质，以免危及这一进展。”警方在圣基尔达地区的电话亭蹲守，希望打电话的人无法抗拒巨额赏金。在等待他再次联系的同时，警方接到了数百个来自公众的电话。成功了吗？请在下周的《罗素街》第二部分中寻找答案，就在Case 4。谢谢。本集暂无评论。点击转录中的任何句子即可发表评论。
